OL,3,GNEWSA'Nothing' done to keep family safe
OL,4,Aafter 999 call
OL,5,
OL,6,FA police officer has admitted "nothing"
OL,7,Fwas done to keep a mother and her four
OL,8,Fchildren safe in the hours before they
OL,9,Fwere murdered in an arson attack.
OL,11,FAt an inquest at Bolton Coroner's
OL,12,FCourt, PC Mike Grundy said he did not
OL,13,Fthink there was a "risk of fire" at the
OL,14,Fhome of Michelle Pearson and her four
OL,15,Fchildren in Walkden, Salford - despite
OL,16,FZak Bolland having made threats to
OL,17,F"petrol bomb" the property.
OL,19,FFour of Michelle's children were
OL,20,Fmurdered in the arson attack on 11
OL,21,FDecember 2017; Michelle, 37, died in
OL,22,FAugust 2019, after being badly burned.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
